; T-0015D golden: rosreestr_cadastr.zmp - RoundEx precision 10 on METRES, proving the
; 15-significant-digit cap (spec F25/table row 18): the 8-digit-integer-part metre values
; leave only 15-8=7 real decimals, so Digits=10 pads 3 trailing zeros - the single most
; likely RoundEx bug per the spec, and the reason this map is on the reviewer's re-derive
; list.
; ResultURL := GetURLBase+RoundEx(GetLMetr,10)+','+RoundEx(GetBMetr,10)+','+
;   RoundEx(GetRMetr,10)+','+RoundEx(GetTMetr,10)
; P3 GetLMetr=-14000817.596939163: 8 integer digits -> round to 15-8=7 decimals
;   (...5969391|63... -> the 8th decimal '6' rounds the 7th digit up: 5969392), pad 3 zeros
;   -> '-14000817.5969392000'.
; P2 GetTMetr=-7.081154551613622e-10 (|v|<1, 1 integer digit '0'): round to 15-1=14 decimals
;   (min(10,14)=10, so a plain round to 10 decimals, no padding) -> '-0.0000000007'.

